\end{aligned}$$B. Content Length vs. Engagement (Data Bucketing)Goal: Determine if longer or shorter posts receive more engagement.Preprocessing: Use the Python script to calculate the length of the content string and store it as a new field, content_length.MongoDB Pipeline:$bucket: Group the posts into custom "buckets" based on content_length (e.g., Short: 0-100 chars, Medium: 101-200 chars, Long: $>200$ chars).$group: Calculate the average engagement_score for each bucket.Visualization: Display this as a bar chart comparing the average engagement across the three length categories.C. Top Tag/Topic Identification (Array Unwinding)Goal: Find the most frequently discussed topics and their median engagement.MongoDB Pipeline:$unwind: Deconstruct the tags array field, creating a separate document for each tag.$group: Group by the tag (_id: "$tags").$sum: Count the total occurrences of each tag (total_posts).$avg: Calculate the average engagement_score for that tag.$sort: Sort the results by total_posts in descending order.$limit: Return the top 10 tags.✅ Deliverables SummarySentiment Calculation: Successfully add a calculated sentiment_score to every document.Web Interface: A basic page displaying the results of the three analyses.Visualization: Charts for:Sentiment over time (Line Chart).Engagement by content length category (Bar Chart).Top 10 most frequent tags (Bar Chart or Word Cloud).
